          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सुतार",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सुतार — sutār — \"a carpenter\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सुताराने नवीन दार बनवलं. sutārāne navīn dār banavlaṁ. The carpenter made a new door."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the past the oblique सुतारा- takes -ने: सुताराने दार बनवलं."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सुतार (sutār) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit sūtradhāra, \"carpenter\" (CDIAL 13563), from sūtra, \"a measuring line\", and dhāra, \"holding\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
